 "id": "opaque/counted-size-share/5m",
 "description": "One request. Message 1 holds 100 text tokens and two thinking blocks of 3,000 signature bytes each, counted at 750 tokens each (1,500 for the position). The operator drops the first block and reports a size of its 3,000 opaque bytes, with no Size.OpaqueTokens. The size holds half the range's opaque bytes, so it gets half the range's count: 1,500 x 3,000 / 6,000 = 750 tokens saved. The forwarded body is billed 1,000 + 100 + 500 + 750 = 2,350 tokens; the ratio is (2,350 - 750) / 6,400 = 0.25. The share is exact here only because the two counts are equal. With unequal counts it is an estimate, and a host that knows the block's count sets Size.OpaqueTokens (previous case).",
